+# First Boot memory sources and authored adaptations
+
+Source reviewed: `C:/Users/footb/Downloads/Echos_Within_Structured_Edition.docx`, 2,271,078 bytes, last modified 2026-10-23. The review read `word/document.xml`; it did not copy the manuscript into the engine, player package or checkpoint.
+
+Locators below use **XML-Pn**, the one-based Word body-paragraph index including empty paragraphs. This edition has 1,315 body paragraphs and 1,209 nonempty paragraphs. Older planning locators use zero-based nonempty paragraphs; neither locator is a printed page number.
+
+| Selected memory | Source locator and older locator | Intended meaning | Proposed presentation |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| A pencil preserves memory | XML-P332, *Adam My Brother Always*; older 289 | Preserving the relationship matters more than possessions. | Ordinary pencil and optional selected writing at the worktable. Record, Trace and Sketch are newly authored mechanics. |
+| Home with Mom and Adam | XML-P1165, *Whole Life Until God*; older 1065 | Remembered safety and belonging. | Dependable hub threshold and return space, without claiming to reconstruct an actual house. Reflective/spiritual dialogue is not an authenticated recording. |
+| Adam recognized Brett's strengths | XML-P327, *Adam My Brother Always*; older 284 | Encouragement without demanding self-promotion. | Newly authored encouragement after building or repairing. |
+| Safety and admiration | XML-P1166, *Whole Life Until God*; older 1066 | Brett admires Adam's writing and intelligence and remembers feeling safe with him. | Writing seat, comfortable silence and steady guidance. |
+| Joy in Adam's happiness | XML-P316, *Light In This World*; older 275 | Shared happiness and generosity; the passage expressly avoids ranking family members. | Optional warm and playful space, without an affection meter. |
+| Turning bad toward good | XML-P1145, *Whole Life Until God*; older 1047 | A lesson Brett attributes to Adam. | Repairing damaged infrastructure for a useful purpose is an adaptation. |
+| Red electric toy truck | XML-P69; older 61 | A happy fragment within a painful passage. | Optional small red model or later vehicle reference; do not automatically stage the surrounding event. |
+| Gaming equipment | XML-P331, *Adam My Brother Always*; older 288 | Describes Brett's equipment ownership. | An authored shared-play corner may draw inspiration from it. XML-P70/older 62 uses conditional Madden language and does not confirm a specific shared gaming incident. |
+
+Jenison's unwanted, hostile starting-base role comes from the creator's explicit game direction. The reviewed edition has no literal Jenison occurrence. Rooms, electrical arcs, sockets, quests, enemy behavior and branch consequences are game fiction. The Caretaker is explicitly fictional, without a real-person or composite biography. Do not infer that differently named book figures refer to the same person.
+
+The creator-selected lines “I'm here. Start with what still responds.” and “That connection holds. We can build from here.” are authored game dialogue. They are not book quotations or recovered recordings.
+
+Adam remains supportive through failure, bypasses, declined help and changed plans. Personal memory is optional and never a progression currency. Danger cues take priority over confirmations and lore; obsolete cues and repetitive chatter should be suppressed. Essential text and cues work offline.
+
+Current world state, committed gameplay recall, preserved source evidence and generated proposals remain distinct. A bypass does not imply that the original fault was repaired. A dismantled path can remain a historical memory without being described as currently usable. Removing a room anchor cannot delete Adam's identity or history.
+
+Status: **source locators VERIFIED; room layouts and presentation PROPOSED**. This source note does not establish implemented chapter gameplay, voice production or a generated narrative service.
