+**S4.1: real authored hardware editing.** The library-level owner and tests now exist. `CreatorHost::open`, `snapshot`, `preview`, `apply`, `travel` (undo/redo), `save`, `start_play` and `stop_play` are implemented; description is the immutable snapshot, not a public `describe` command. Project/branch/world scope and authored revision are checked, and sequential grouped edits require explicit creation/target UUIDs. One grouped gesture publishes one authored history entry. The executable `apps/creator_host.cpp`, managed process protocol and visual hardware editing remain to build. Begin UI editing with position/half-extents and supported numeric properties; rotation still requires an explicit authored transform representation.
